| 0x28    | OUT1        | RO          | Ciphertext [95:64]                 |
| 0x2C    | OUT2        | RO          | Ciphertext [63:32]                 |
| 0x30    | OUT3        | RO          | Ciphertext [31:0]                  |


2. ACCESS TYPE
--------------

RW = Read/Write
    The CPU can write the register and read its stored value.

RO = Read Only
    The CPU can read the register. The value is generated by hardware.

RW/RO = Field-dependent access
    Different fields within the same register have different access types.


3. 0x00 : CTRL_STATUS
---------------------

The 32-bit CTRL_STATUS register is divided into:

    Bits [31:16] = STATUS
    Bits [15:0]  = CONTROL


STATUS [31:16]
--------------

| Bit   | Name     | Access | Description                           |
|-------|----------|--------|---------------------------------------|
| 16    | DONE     | RO     | AES Cipher operation completed        |
| 17    | KDONE    | RO     | AES Inverse Cipher key load completed |
| 31:18 | RESERVED | RO     | Reserved; read as 0                  |


STATUS field:

    31                    18 17       16
    +-----------------------+----+------+
    |       RESERVED        |KDONE| DONE |
    +-----------------------+----+------+
             STATUS [31:16]


CONTROL [15:0]
--------------

| Bit   | Name     | Access | Description                         |
|-------|----------|--------|-------------------------------------|
| 0     | LD       | RW     | Load/start AES Cipher operation     |
| 1     | KLD      | RW     | Load key for AES Inverse Cipher     |
| 2     | RST      | RW     | Reset AES operation/control         |
| 15:3 | RESERVED | RW     | Reserved; write as 0               |


CONTROL field:

    15                     3  2    1    0
    +-----------------------+----+----+----+
    |       RESERVED        | RST| KLD| LD |
    +-----------------------+----+----+----+
             CONTROL [15:0]


