7. AES SIGNAL-TO-REGISTER MAPPING
---------------------------------

| AES Signal | Register Field       | Direction |
|------------|----------------------|-----------|
| LD         | CTRL_STATUS[0]       | CPU -> AES |
| KLD        | CTRL_STATUS[1]       | CPU -> AES |
| RST        | CTRL_STATUS[2]       | CPU -> AES |
| DONE       | CTRL_STATUS[16]      | AES -> CPU |
| KDONE      | CTRL_STATUS[17]      | AES -> CPU |
| KEY[127:0] | KEY0-KEY3            | CPU -> AES |
| TEXT_IN    | TEXT0-TEXT3          | CPU -> AES |
| TEXT_OUT   | OUT0-OUT3            | AES -> CPU |


8. ENCRYPTION OPERATION
-----------------------

1. CPU writes the 128-bit AES key into KEY0–KEY3.
2. CPU writes the plaintext into TEXT0–TEXT3.
3. CPU sets LD = 1 in CTRL_STATUS[0].
4. AES Cipher receives the load/start command.
5. AES Cipher performs the encryption.
6. AES Cipher asserts DONE when the operation is complete.
7. CTRL_STATUS[16] reflects DONE.
8. CPU reads OUT0–OUT3 to obtain the ciphertext.


9. DECRYPTION OPERATION
-----------------------

1. CPU writes the 128-bit AES key into KEY0–KEY3.
2. CPU sets KLD = 1 in CTRL_STATUS[1].
3. AES Inverse Cipher performs key expansion.
4. AES Inverse Cipher asserts KDONE when key loading is complete.
5. CTRL_STATUS[17] reflects KDONE.
6. CPU provides the ciphertext through TEXT0–TEXT3.
7. The AES Inverse Cipher performs decryption.
8. The decrypted plaintext is available through OUT0–OUT3.


